A||||3||Kasdan||Double Kill Story||||5||
Z||000000||Kasdan||09-07-2001||09:22 AM||||Yesterday, i pulled up to a stoplight behind a 2000 Honda Civic Sedan.  Not only was this a Civic Sedan, but this was one of those elusive Type-R Sedans.  Complete with tinted windows, a 6 foot spoiler, and a bumblebee muffler, i proceded to follow him down a hill, with him accelerating as fast as he could, and with me riding his you know what.  We lined up at the nest stoplight, and he revved his non-vtec Civic DX Type-R Sedan and the bumbleebee buzzed around furiously.  Its furious, but sure not fast.  We take off, him gringing the clutch with every shift, backfiring all the way.  we went to 100mph approx, and needless to say, i burned up some rice.  Well, i slow down to make a turn, and my engine suddenly overhears and starts knocking hard.  Not only did i kill a ricer, but i threw a rod and killed my GT.  Double kill!<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||5
Z||000001||Urchin||09-07-2001||12:32 PM||||Ouch, sorry to hear that.  Well, if it was going to happen, at least you were having fun at the time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">  <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Butter||09-07-2001||02:58 PM||||Just goes to show that at least over 23 year old American Iron can beat at least 1 year old Jap Crap even on a bad day.  Too bad you had to use up what is left of your GT burning rice. Remember the statement before each episode of the 6 Million Dollar Man.<P>Disclaimer:<BR>I started out working on Honda's and I like them but I still call them Jap Crap.  I ride and enjoy a dune buggy made with Mexican Mess and German Gue so yall don't go flamin' me unless we can all laugh at the frailties of the engineering involved.||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||09-07-2001||09:37 PM||||Hrm, double kill indeed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>If only Honda made the engines in the fiero (I'm thinking their titanium conrod, 3.0/3.2l 4-cam V6. mmmmmm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Reliable, plenty powerful, and sping way up withought ever quitting.<P>I envy the reliability of that little civic, though absolutely nothing else  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
